0 Der Tokenstrom - the glyphs A4-S03 emits, travels and absorbs
0 Name: token-strom.ldr
0 Author: spex project (hand-authored placement data; not sourced from an official ldraw.org models/ release)
0 // Forty-eight 1x1 bricks in 84 Medium_Nougat - THE SAME PART AND THE SAME
0 // COLOUR AS A2-S03's TOKENS. `recipes/tokens.json` builds Uruk's clay
0 // counters out of 3005.dat in 84 ("lehm"), and what crosses the lattice in
0 // the last act is not a new object: it is that counter, 5300 years later, in
0 // a net that calls it a token for the same reason Uruk did.
0 //
0 // TWO COLOURS WERE TRIED AND MEASURED FIRST, and both failed for reasons
0 // worth keeping. 10 Bright_Green was invisible: `recipes/gitter.json` gives
0 // the lattice's NODES that exact colour and only its edges the translucent
0 // 35, so a green token travelling a lattice of green nodes is a lattice of
0 // green nodes - forty-eight things moved, the probe measured it, and no eye
0 // could see it. 15 White was the opposite failure: at the act's exposure of
0 // 0.6 with bloom on it, every token became a small sun and took the lattice's
0 // colour with it. Clay reads because it differs in HUE rather than in
0 // brightness, which is the one axis this act has spare.
0 //
0 // THESE PLACEMENTS ARE NEVER SEEN. The `tokens` generator overwrites every
0 // position each frame from the lattice's own node grid; this file exists to
0 // say how MANY tokens there are and what they are made of. They are laid out
0 // in a row here purely so the bundle has sane bounds.
0 //
0 // Stage: alongside the lattice at x = 27000 LDU (1350 studs).

